   "text": {
    "L1": "Ila Sachani's story is about skill and determination, not pity.",
    "L2": "She found her own way to embroider with her feet, and she kept trying when threading a needle was hard.",
    "L3": "Her mother and grandmother taught her embroidery, while her family supported her.",
    "L4": "First, Ila was born in a farmer's family in Amreli.",
    "L5": "Then her work was shown at a state exhibition, where people saw and bought it.",
    "L6": "Her success grew, and she received many awards, including the President's Medal.",
    "L7": "Her craft brought regular income and new independence. The message is that focus, hard work, positivity and never giving up can turn challenges into victories.",
    "L8": "Now put the main events in the correct order."
   },
